# Mise en (Expo) — project conventions

- **Target:** Android only. iOS is not supported or tested.
- **Stack:** Expo SDK 54, React Native 0.81, TypeScript **strict**.
- **UI:** Functional components only; no class components. Every interactive
  element needs `accessibilityLabel` + `accessibilityRole`, and stateful ones
  need `accessibilityState`.
- **Design system:** Build screens from `components/ui` (`Screen`, `Button`,
  `IconButton`, `Card`, `Chip`, `TextField`, `SegmentedControl`, `SwitchRow`,
  `Text`, `ModalCard`, `Section`, `ImageScrim`). Do not hand-roll a `Pressable`
  that one of these already covers.
- **Styling:** Spacing, radii, type and elevation come from `theme/tokens.ts`;
  colours from `theme/colors.ts`. **No raw numbers** for padding, margin, gap,
  `borderRadius` or `fontSize` (bare `Text` and `fontFamily` strings included),
  and **no hex literals** outside `theme/`. The one exception is a radius that
  is half a known pixel size, to make a circle.
- **Touch feedback:** Every `Pressable` needs `android_ripple={ripple(...)}`
  plus `pressedStyle(pressed)` from `components/ui/press`. Targets are 48dp
  minimum; use `hitSlopFor(size)` when the control must look smaller.
- **Elevation:** Use `elevation(level, resolved)` from `theme/tokens.ts`. Never
  set `shadowOpacity`/`shadowRadius` directly — Android ignores them, and dark
  mode gets its depth from borders and `surfaceMuted` instead.
- **Contrast:** Text on a filled control uses the matching `on*` token
  (`onPrimaryFill`, `onPrimarySoft`, `onDestructiveFill`), never `'#fff'`. The
  pairs in `theme/colors.ts` are chosen to clear WCAG AA in both modes.
- **Storage:** `expo-sqlite` for all structured recipe data; `expo-file-system` for cook photos; `expo-secure-store` for appearance and onboarding preferences.
- **Secrets:** API keys currently come from `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` env vars, which Metro
  **inlines into the shipped bundle** — they are not secret. Do not commit build
  output. Moving to a proxy or per-user keys in `expo-secure-store` is open work.
- **Networking:** always go through `lib/http.ts` so requests carry a timeout.
- **Units:** Persist **metric only** (`g`, `kg`, `ml`, `l`, `cm`, `°C`, `tsp`, `tbsp` as needed). No imperial in stored data.
- **Scaling:** Ingredients are structured objects; step text uses placeholders + `scalableQuantities` from import — do not regex-replace quantities in free text at runtime.
- **Networking:** OpenAI for import + recipe-scoped chat only; use `@react-native-community/netinfo` for offline UX.
- **Imports:** Prefer path alias `@/` for app root where configured.
